{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator decision (2026-11-19 PST): option (1). On Windows only, rebar writes an owner-only DACL on the temporary op-cert key copy it creates for signing, so that Win32-OpenSSH accepts it and op-cert signing works on Windows. Principle: anyone can sign, so no platform is excluded. This does not change the nymph decision, which covers the persistent key file (rely on the default ACL). The 28 tests in `openssh-key-acl.args` return to the Windows sweep."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795109818495387399,"uuid":"018abd5b-d89f-4ab0-87b5-4e35ae011c5c"}